WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.682 --> 00:00:03.062
Eh, this one happen to everybody.

2
00:00:03.082 --> 00:00:06.982
You write a function, you run it, the screen show 120.

3
00:00:07.002 --> 00:00:10.492
Correct answer! But the test say FAIL, got None.

4
00:00:11.002 --> 00:00:12.822
Wah lau, how come?

5
00:00:12.842 --> 00:00:15.212
The answer is right there on the screen what.

6
00:00:15.246 --> 00:00:17.146
Today we settle functions lah.

7
00:00:17.166 --> 00:00:19.256
How def and calling work.

8
00:00:19.326 --> 00:00:23.666
Parameter versus argument. Return versus print, this one the exam love

9
00:00:23.686 --> 00:00:27.346
sia. Then the None trap, and local scope.

10
00:00:27.366 --> 00:00:30.696
After this, you know exactly why that test fail.

11
00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:37.559
Step 1. def to_minutes, with hours inside the brackets.

12
00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:40.999
Then the body: return hours times 60.

13
00:00:41.019 --> 00:00:43.079
This def ah, only a RECIPE.

14
00:00:43.099 --> 00:00:44.469
Nothing cook yet.

15
00:00:44.539 --> 00:00:48.799
Step 2: you write to_minutes with no brackets.

16
00:00:48.819 --> 00:00:50.839
Only the name, nothing run.

17
00:00:50.859 --> 00:00:54.919
Step 3: to_minutes 2, WITH brackets.

18
00:00:54.939 --> 00:00:59.163
Now the body run, hours is 2, you get 120.

19
00:00:59.183 --> 00:01:01.563
Got 2 words you must know.

20
00:01:01.583 --> 00:01:04.883
hours, the name in the def line, is the PARAMETER.

21
00:01:04.903 --> 00:01:07.923
The 2 you pass in the call is the argument.

22
00:01:07.943 --> 00:01:11.993
Python match them by position: first to first, second to second.

23
00:01:12.214 --> 00:01:16.363
The trap: take a function describe, with name and age.

24
00:01:16.383 --> 00:01:20.203
You swap the 2 arguments, Python usually never complain.

25
00:01:20.223 --> 00:01:22.633
It just give you the wrong thing, quietly.

26
00:01:22.863 --> 00:01:26.963
Unless you NAME them in the call, like age equals 19.

27
00:01:26.983 --> 00:01:29.193
Then the order no longer matter.

28
00:01:31.277 --> 00:01:34.807
Now the big one: return versus print.

29
00:01:34.877 --> 00:01:37.977
Print SHOW the value on the screen, and then the call

30
00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:42.017
is worth None. Return HAND the value back to the caller,

31
00:01:42.037 --> 00:01:44.127
and the function stop at once.

32
00:01:44.301 --> 00:01:49.657
Try it: total equals to_minutes 2 plus to_minutes 1.

33
00:01:49.677 --> 00:01:54.937
With return, that is 120 plus 60, so 180.

34
00:01:54.957 --> 00:01:59.497
With print, the screen show 120 and 60, but both calls

35
00:01:59.517 --> 00:02:02.087
worth None. None plus None?

36
00:02:02.197 --> 00:02:02.887
TypeError!

37
00:02:03.166 --> 00:02:06.898
Why ah? Because print is for your EYES, return is for

38
00:02:06.918 --> 00:02:07.848
the program.

39
00:02:07.998 --> 00:02:10.168
Tests cannot see your screen.

40
00:02:10.879 --> 00:02:12.409
And the None trap.

41
00:02:12.639 --> 00:02:16.619
Function reach the end, never meet a return, Python give back

42
00:02:16.639 --> 00:02:17.609
None for you.

43
00:02:17.839 --> 00:02:21.219
Look at sign of n: if n is 0 or more,

44
00:02:21.239 --> 00:02:23.369
return plus. Negative n?

45
00:02:23.439 --> 00:02:25.449
Fall off the end, get None.

46
00:02:25.599 --> 00:02:28.569
So check EVERY path end with a return.

47
00:02:30.643 --> 00:02:32.863
Last idea, local scope.

48
00:02:32.883 --> 00:02:39.583
make_total 4, 5. Inside: result equals a plus b, then return

49
00:02:39.603 --> 00:02:42.223
result. Outside, you print result.

50
00:02:42.243 --> 00:02:42.993
Can or not?

51
00:02:43.981 --> 00:02:45.734
Cannot! NameError.

52
00:02:45.897 --> 00:02:48.664
Why ah? Because result is LOCAL.

53
00:02:48.684 --> 00:02:51.264
It is born when the call start, and gone when the

54
00:02:51.284 --> 00:02:55.424
call end. The 9 did come back, but nobody catch it.

55
00:02:55.444 --> 00:03:00.384
So catch it lah: total equals make_total 4, 5.

56
00:03:00.404 --> 00:03:03.854
What you need outside, you must return, then store.

57
00:03:05.867 --> 00:03:11.367
The one-line takeaway: def only define, return HAND back, print only

58
00:03:11.387 --> 00:03:12.157
show.

59
00:03:12.187 --> 00:03:15.127
So that test at the start fail because the function print

60
00:03:15.147 --> 00:03:17.927
120 but return nothing.

61
00:03:17.947 --> 00:03:22.407
And for from-scratch questions, same recipe every time: put your loop

62
00:03:22.427 --> 00:03:26.487
inside a def, the data become the parameter, the last print

63
00:03:26.507 --> 00:03:28.837
become a return, AFTER the loop.

64
00:03:29.136 --> 00:03:33.527
The practice notebook got 6 core exercises: 3 to predict, 2

65
00:03:33.547 --> 00:03:36.567
fix the bug, and 1 where you turn a loop program

66
00:03:36.587 --> 00:03:40.571
into a function. Got extra practice also, if you want more.

67
00:03:40.591 --> 00:03:44.251
Last thing: graded work must be your OWN, the course does

68
00:03:44.271 --> 00:03:45.891
not allow AI on it.

69
00:03:45.911 --> 00:03:49.264
Practise here until steady, then that one you do yourself.

70
00:03:49.284 --> 00:03:50.121
Jia you!
